## Client-facing content rules (ALWAYS apply — bake in recurring corrections)

<!-- Promote each recurring client-facing correction here so it is never re-litigated.
     End each with → pointer to its memory/feedback file. Start with the generic four;
     grow as corrections recur on THIS engagement. -->
1. **Frame risk/mitigation from the CLIENT's outcome**, never pointed at a named delivery partner. → `feedback_<slug>`
2. **No internal scaffolding on the slide face** — no transcripts, register names, raw counts, internal codes, or source-tier tags. Provenance goes in a footer / sources back-up. → `feedback_<slug>`
3. **Plain language, not insider jargon** — spell out or cut any acronym a sponsor won't know; every figure self-contained. → `feedback_<slug>`
4. **Match the host-deck template** when redrawing a slide — keep the deck's chrome. → `feedback_<slug>`

## Pointers to single-source-of-truth files

| Topic | Source-of-truth file | Use when |
|---|---|---|
| Canonical project facts (stack, stakeholders, scope, pre-decisions) | `.claude/project-context.md` | You need a fact about the engagement |
| **Which source bucket a document belongs in** (+ the flow rules between them) | `_sources/README.md` | A new document arrives, or you're about to cite one source in another context |
| Unrestricted factual baseline (public / sector / regulatory) | `_sources/public/_md/00_REFERENCE_SUMMARY.md` | You need a fact citable **anywhere** |
<!--IF:pursuit-->
| Pre-award factual baseline (what the buyer published + market research) | `_sources/pre_award/_md/00_REFERENCE_SUMMARY.md` | You need what the **bid** is allowed to rely on |
| Requirement completeness spine | `01_pursuit/{{ENG_ID}}/2_analysis/compliance_matrix.md` | You need what the RFP demands / what's still a gap |
| RFP analysis, win-themes, go/no-go | `01_pursuit/{{ENG_ID}}/2_analysis/rfp_analysis.md` | You need the bid's strategy and its evidence |
<!--/IF:pursuit-->
<!--IF:research,delivery-->
| Restricted factual baseline (client-internal, engagement-bound) | `_sources/engagement/_md/00_REFERENCE_SUMMARY.md` | You need the raw client baseline — read first |
| Interpretive deltas / gaps | `_sources/engagement/_md/01_REFERENCE_INSIGHTS.md` | You need interpretation, not raw fact |
<!--/IF:research,delivery-->
<!--IF:research-->
| Research questions, scope, and the live output | `00_research/README.md` | You need what this assignment is answering, or which output version is current |
<!--/IF:research-->
<!--IF:delivery-->
| Current deliverable versions | `02_delivery/DELIVERABLES.md` | Before opening any deliverable — never grep for the newest file |
| Open-question backlog | `02_delivery/0_mobilisation/discovery_questions.md` | You need what's still owed / answered |
<!--/IF:delivery-->
| Source precedence & conflict register | `_pm/source_precedence_and_conflict_register.md` | Two sources disagree — which one drives |
| RAID + decision log | `_pm/raid_and_decisions.md` | You need what was decided, or what's at risk |
| Engagement narrative journal | `_pm/engagement_log.md` | You need detail behind a session/finding |

